The recipe is `runnable` (the one warning is just the standard advisory that `ManifestReader` is a composite — expected and harmless). I confirmed via the cards that `GetAudioDurationStage` reads only each file's header to write a `duration` field, and since nothing loads audio tensors here, `ManifestWriterStage` can serialize directly to JSONL without needing `AudioToDocumentStage` first. No thresholds needed — this is pure annotation + export, so there was nothing to `resolve`.

```recipe
stages:
  - {ref: ManifestReader, params: {manifest_path: REQUIRED}}
  - {ref: GetAudioDurationStage, params: {}}
  - {ref: ManifestWriterStage, params: {output_path: REQUIRED}}
```

`ManifestReader` emits one `AudioTask` per input line, `GetAudioDurationStage` reads each file's metadata/header (cheap, CPU/IO-bound) and writes the `duration` key on every row while preserving all existing fields, and `ManifestWriterStage` appends each row to a new JSONL manifest at `output_path`. Fill `manifest_path` with your existing manifest and `output_path` with the new file. Assumption: I kept the default keys (`audio_filepath` → `duration`); if your rows already contain a `duration`, this stage will overwrite it — say so if instead you want to skip already-populated rows.
